{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790964149,"nonce":"Fi167tbT/VZqBWni5m3AiiIX7Ok=","message":"Status of the rewrite, which is in the working tree and not yet committed:\n\n- crates/hlwindow is the adapter. Its build.rs runs xwindow_backend::install and xwindow_bindgen::generate(Runtime::HashLink), and writes crates/hlwindow/haxe/window. Its runtime module is hl_xidl, shared with hlwgpu.\n- Under Ash (~/.ash/bin/ash, 2026-10-02), a visible window took synthetic mouse and keyboard input on macOS. Clicks, the wheel, keys with their supplements, modifiers, focus, cursor-entered and device events all arrived as nested Haxe enums.\n- The window was handed to xgpu through GpuInstance.surface(platform, raw 0..3) and drew a triangle for 78 frames.\n- scripts/build_window_wasm.sh builds xwindow.wasm (216 KB) and its two page modules. ash --build loads it into a wasm32-wasip1-threads program under `ash run`, but not in a page, because Ash's browser host loads no side modules (ash aca00a17e33c6222153a05745f9682e22f98507f2094b88e99248c9bdb0e8670).\n- Pushing waits on b699cc4d07f67f721d433bf672b84a59289f4ae1059dec775d0096350398010b: the workspace currently resolves xwindow, xgpu and x-idl from sibling checkouts.","files":null}]}